From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:51:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] phys/TEMPO: TEMPO water-closure series (round 2) on
 881614f

TEMPO 881614f creates water: in em_quarter_ss (supercell, doubly
periodic, no surface fluxes, 2 h, mp_physics=88) domain water plus
accumulated precipitation grows by +1.111e-2 of the precipitation, and
the per-call meter in WRF's dry mass shows +1.167e-2 from TEMPO alone.

Moves the submodule to 881614f plus the three round-2 TEMPO commits
(closing the water budget: settling, graupel re-closure, sedimentation
density, clips and surface threshold; semi-Lagrangian sedimentation falls
back to piecewise constant on a negative edge; water at or below r1 goes
to vapour instead of being deleted). The submodule tree is identical to
git am of the exported round-2 patches on 881614f.

Measured in em_quarter_ss, 2 h, mp_physics=88:
- per-call meter (WRF dry mass): +1.167e-2 -> -1.385e-4 of precipitation;
  in TEMPO's own density: +1.181e-2 -> +8.2e-7 (the remainder is the
  layer-mass mismatch, fixed in the next commit);
- domain W+P residual at 2 h: +1.111e-2 -> -7.22e-4 of precipitation
  (round 1 of the series: -7.03e-4).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
